        <mxCell id="cross_text" parent="1" style="text;html=1;fontSize=11;fontColor=#1A1A1A;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=4;" value="&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;What this system does (one sentence):&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Reads a helpdesk ticket, retrieves the most relevant policy chunks from a Bedrock Knowledge Base built over uploaded policy documents (SharePoint AUP, Zscaler ZIA policy export), reasons with a foundation model whether the issue is a cross-domain policy conflict, and posts the finding to Teams as an Adaptive Card.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Bedrock Guardrails sit in front of the model and intercept tickets that violate restricted topics (credential sharing, security control bypass).&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="160" width="660" x="638" y="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
